{% comment %}
  sections/home-marquee.liquid
  Ported from the "Arcane Flame Website Prototype" option-c.html:
    - CSS: lines ~179-186 (.marquee, .marquee__track, .marquee__track span,
      .marquee__track span::after, @keyframes slide) — see
      shopify-theme/assets/home-marquee.css for the full colour-substitution
      notes.
    - Markup: lines ~508-514 (<div class="marquee">...</div>), the 8-item
      scrolling claims strip between the hero and the detail/craft section.

  The prototype's 8 claim strings (`<span>12K Resin Detail</span>` etc.) are
  hardcoded markup. Here they're a repeatable `marquee_item` block (one
  `text` setting each) so a merchant can add, remove, reorder or edit claims
  from the theme editor. The 8 default preset blocks below reproduce the
  prototype's current default list verbatim, in the same order.

  Seamless-loop technique: the prototype duplicates the track's content at
  runtime via JS (`mq.innerHTML += mq.innerHTML`, option-c.html line 828)
  so `@keyframes slide{to{transform:translateX(-50%)}}` has two copies of
  the content to slide across, landing exactly on the second copy's start
  with no visible seam. That doubling is done here in Liquid instead — the
  block loop below runs twice in sequence, rendering every block's markup
  twice inside the same .marquee__track — so no JS is needed and the effect
  works identically for merchant-edited (including short) block lists.
  Verified with both the default 8-item list and a 3-item list; see the
  task report for the seam-test results.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="marquee" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="marquee__track" id="Marquee-{{ section.id }}">
    {% for block in section.blocks %}
      <span {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ block.settings.text }}</span>
    {% endfor %}
    {% for block in section.blocks %}
      <span aria-hidden="true">{{ block.settings.text }}</span>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>

